  annotation "note_1771591086914_1", anchor: "learned the technique judging her colony could not depend on a single practitioner", text: "She was right. Promenade Hei survived. I wrote about her thermal decline in the Lianhinglou entry — the stepped cooling, the illegible flipper-mark. She made the calculation and it was correct. The colony outlived her clarity. That is not a tragedy. It is exactly what she paid for.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771591086914_2", anchor: "No formal account survives of what those wartime practitioners became", text: "Stratum 4 preserves three sets of thermal impressions from the late Incursion period that match Shell Hatch crystal-array resonance patterns. Two show aurora-glow signatures so saturated the surrounding ice fluoresces when re-examined under controlled light. The third is colder than the substrate — body temperature below ambient. Whatever those wartime practitioners became, the ice remembers them. Formal accounts are not the only kind.", type: :correction, display: :full
